WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.980
<i>Today is February 14th, Valentine's Day.</i>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.980
<b>Valentine's Night
Aigasa Kurisu
Reading of the Soul</b>

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:10.360
<i>Holmes-san and I were invited by a 
certain writer to visit Yoshida-Sanso.</i>

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.610
What a wonderful cafe!

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.110
It really is lovely, isn't it?

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:20.160
The Shinkokan of Yoshida-Sanso 
was built in the early Showa era.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.120
The way it reflects the classic architecture 
out front is one of its main features.

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:26.330
Aoi-san?

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.630
Oh, sorry. I was just remembering 
what you said the other day...

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.130
Aigasa Kurisu?

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.070
That mystery writer?

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:35.630
Yes.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.690
My editor used to work with her.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:44.560
She's hosting a book reading
 on Valentine's Day

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.540
and asked me to invite Kiyotaka.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.500
I know it's a special day, so I'm sorry,

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.400
but she seems to want your advice.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.840
This is detective work, then?

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.650
I'm not exactly enthusiastic...

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:03.660
She's apparently holding it 
at the Shinkokan in Yoshida-Sanso.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:05.160
Yoshida-Sanso?

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:06.760
I'll do it!

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:10.800
You just love cafes, don't you, Holmes-san?

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.800
I have a second stomach 
for cafes, you could say.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:18.390
<i>I don't think that's how that goes...</i>

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:37.740
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:53.900
Valentine's Party

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:53.900
Episode 11

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.000
I can't wait for the reading tonight.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.000
Indeed.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.880
Aoi-san, I see you've started 
drinking your coffee black.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.780
Oh, yeah.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:08.330
Lately, I've even started 
appreciating the flavor.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.510
You've really grown up, Aoi-san.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:13.000
Oh, I wouldn't say that...

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.040
And so, this is for you.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.140
Are you okay?

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.520
I'm sorry.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.000
Th-That's okay...

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.320
It seems that the other guests have arrived.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.060
S-So it does...

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:34.050
Would you be Ijuin-sensei's son?

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.320
Yes, I'm Yagashira Kiyotaka.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:40.080
I'm Hashimoto, Ijuin-sensei's editor.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.030
Ijuin-sensei (Takeshi)'s Supervising Editor
Hashimoto

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.370
This must be quite an imposition for you.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:45.230
Now, who's this young lady?

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:48.080
I'm Mashiro Aoi. I work part-time at Kura.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:51.580
Hashimoto-san.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.830
You appear to be married,

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:55.760
but you came alone tonight?

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:58.340
Yes... My wife is pregnant.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.840
<i>He doesn't look very happy...</i>

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:03.390
Hashimoto-san, were you going to hit on her?

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:04.490
You creep.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.880
I can't catch a break with you, can I?

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:09.100
And who might these be, Hashimoto-san?

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:12.370
Friends of Aigasa-sensei's from high school,

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:15.470
Iijima Suzuka-san and Ooishi Kumi-san.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.850
Aigasa-sensei's Friend
Iijima Suzuka

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.110
Aigasa-sensei's Friend
Ooishi Kumi

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:17.710
I'm Suzuka. Nice to meet you!

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:18.360
A pleasure.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:21.080
C'mon, Ma-kun, introduce yourself!

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:24.110
N-Nice to meet you. I'm Oda Masashi.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.110
Photographer
Oda Masashi

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:28.620
<b>The Butterfly That Fell to Heaven
Aigasa Kurisu</b>

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.310
Ma-kun is Aigasa Kurisu's 
personal photographer!

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:32.430
He designs her official website, too!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:34.250
<b>Aigasa</b>

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:34.250
He's amazing!

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:36.080
I wouldn't say that...

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:39.250
Oh? When did you become such a hot property?

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.380
Kikuchi-sensei, p-please don't tease me!

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.600
I'm Kikuchi, a photographer.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.590
Photographer
Kikuchi

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:48.390
I handle Aigasa-sensei's 
photography, along with Oda.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:53.720
In other words, everyone here tonight
 is involved with Aigasa-sensei somehow?

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.400
Sheesh... The hell is this all about?

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.610
Does that mean he is, too?

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.400
No, I don't know him.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.900
I'm Detective Komatsu.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.900
Private Detective
Komatsu

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:08.370
A detective? What are you 
doing at this reading?

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.720
That's what I'd like to know.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.320
Aigasa Kurisu asked me to 
investigate something,

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:14.790
but she stiffed me on the bill.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.760
Then she told me to come to this reading.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.290
What on earth could she...

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:24.300
It appears we're about to start.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:28.300
I see everybody's here.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.800
<i>Huh? It's not the author?</i>

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:40.560
We'll now begin Aigasa Kurisu's
 "Reading of the Soul."

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:46.820
I, Inoue Kana, younger sister of Inoue Rika,
 will perform the reading.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.580
Inoue Rika?

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:51.960
Aigasa Kurisu's real name, I assume.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.890
It seems she styles herself 
after Agatha Christie.

00:05:54.890 --> 00:05:55.830
I see...

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.830
"One day, I was killed.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.840
I did not kill myself.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.340
Somebody killed me.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.340
And the one who did it...

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:11.140
is one of you gathered here tonight."

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:14.350
<i>Is that it?</i>

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:19.100
Kana-san, this is in pretty bad taste.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.860
Y-Yeah!

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.110
I thought this was about 
celebrating Rika's recovery.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:24.590
Yagashira-san.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:27.360
Allow me to explain.

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:30.360
During the full moon one month ago,

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:34.870
my sister attempted suicide in front 
of the condo where she works.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.120
But through either good luck or bad, 
the ribbon she hanged herself with snapped.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:41.880
The trees below broke her fall,

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:44.170
which saved her life.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.200
She left a note,

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.510
so I thought she really was 
trying to kill herself.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:54.760
But when she regained consciousness, 
she told me this...

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:58.520
I would never try to kill myself!

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:01.080
Someone tried to murder me!

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:04.900
The people who were present 
the day of the incident:

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:06.900
Suzuka-san, Kumi-san.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.150
The people who called her just 
before the suicide attempt:

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.160
Kikuchi-san, Oda-san.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:14.910
And the people with whom 
she had personal quarrels:

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:17.160
Hashimoto-san, Komatsu-san.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:20.120
I believe one of you is the culprit.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:21.170
Hang on a minute!

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:24.320
She's the one who stiffed <i>me</i>!

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:26.170
I'm the victim here!

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:30.420
And Kumi and I only went to see 
Rika because we were worried!

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.380
You've got us wrong, too.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:33.780
We had no reason to quarrel.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:37.030
We've butted heads over work before,

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:39.430
but that's no reason to kill her.

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:42.600
Besides, didn't Rika see the killer's face?

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:43.880
No.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:48.360
But she told me that someone 
definitely pushed her.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:51.450
Is that any reason to treat us like criminals?

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.360
I'm offended.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:58.240
You see, that's why I invited Yagashira-sama, 
the rumored great detective.

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:02.440
I see.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:03.750
I'll take the case.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.710
H-Holmes-san!

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:09.960
But the moment I solve it,

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:13.510
would you kindly spread the word that those 
"great detective" rumors are false?

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.260
Yes, if you wish.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:19.520
<i>He really doesn't like being 
known as a detective...</i>

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:22.520
Then let's get started.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.370
First, Suzuka-san,

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:28.450
could you tell us where you were
 the night of the incident?

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:33.400
That night, Kumi and I went
 to Rika's apartment.

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:37.600
She'd been lashing out a lot,
 so we were worried.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:40.760
<i>Lashing out? Does that mean...</i>

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.540
Was this regarding Hashimoto-san?

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:44.520
Oh, you could tell?

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:47.970
Kana-san mentioned
 they had a personal quarrel,

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.960
so I thought his marriage
 might be the cause.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.500
That's right.

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:53.460
But that's just how Rika is.

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:57.480
She gets these strange ideas
and then takes it out on everyone else.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:58.550
I see.

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:03.310
Next, tell me how you met Rika.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:06.810
We were on the library committee
 together in high school.

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:09.820
We have totally different personalities,

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:12.940
but we shared a love of reading,

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.700
so we became fast friends.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.450
And you maintained that
 friendship after graduating?

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:22.620
No, we lost touch after graduation.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:26.720
We only connected again when Rika 
applied for the newcomer award.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.460
And why was that?

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:32.960
She was going to submit a revised version
of a story she'd written in high school,

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.720
so she called us to check some things.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.780
After that, we started meeting up 
more and more often.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:41.220
What did you think when 
Rika-san won that award?

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:45.600
Well... "congratulations," of course.

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:47.040
I understand.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:48.600
This concludes my questions for you.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.390
The night of the incident?

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:52.190
Suzuka told you, I'm sure.

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:53.610
We went to see Rika.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:56.110
Then tell me about how you met.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:57.720
I'm sure you've heard already.

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:59.360
On the library committee in high school.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:09:59.870
Yes.

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:04.620
And you all decided to write 
stories together, didn't you?

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:06.620
<i>Huh? Did she say that?</i>

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.370
Suzuka told you about that, too?

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.460
We were full of youthful passion.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.880
She probably told you, but they 
were all absolutely dreadful.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.140
Suzuka came up with fun characters,

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:21.640
but she couldn't tell a story to save her life.

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:24.800
I liked thinking up gimmicks,

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:26.890
but I could never finish anything.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.620
Rika was the most solid of us,

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:31.910
but her stories just weren't that interesting.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.680
<i>Wow, harsh...</i>

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:40.120
I gotta say, I was shocked when I 
saw her newcomer award interview.

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:41.530
What do you mean?

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:44.400
Rika's usually totally plain.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:46.040
R-Really?

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:47.540
See?

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:51.040
Sh-She's like a different person...

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:54.990
Really? She looks exactly the same to me.

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:58.460
By the way, who picked out her costume?

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.800
Oda-san the photographer, I think.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:06.810
Yes, Aigasa-sensei and I always came 
up with the photo shoot costumes.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.530
The costuming and makeup are quite novel.

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:12.310
What gave you the idea?

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:14.370
During the interview, she started crying.

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:18.090
She said she didn't want to appear 
in the magazine as she was.

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:19.920
Huh? Why not?

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:20.820
The truth is...

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.310
My sister was bullied in the past.

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:28.080
She didn't want the world 
to see her as her old self.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.710
And so we came up with an image for her

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:34.120
to better match the voice of her books.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:38.040
She thought of the costume 
as a sort of disguise.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:43.250
Then you also came up with the costume and setting
used on the day of the incident?

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:46.220
Yes, she and I came up with it together.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:47.790
I see.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:50.230
Now, please tell me about 
the night of the incident.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:52.730
U-Um, I think...

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:57.230
Kikuchi-sensei and I were in front 
of her apartment building.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:00.240
We'd come to photograph some things for her homepage.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:05.240
I think... Kikuchi-sensei 
called her twice then.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:08.240
The first time was to go over 
the contents of the shoot.

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:12.870
The second was because he forgot 
to confirm the time of the shoot.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.880
That's why I called her twice.

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:18.380
Did you? I see...

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:21.640
What? Is that different from what Oda said?

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:24.060
No, he said the same thing.

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:26.310
Glad to hear it.

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:32.140
By the way, did you have a personal
 relationship with Aigasa-sensei?

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:34.860
No, not me.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:37.580
Aigasa-san liked Oda,

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.650
so the three of us had 
lots of dinners together.

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:42.150
<i>But I thought Rika-san...</i>

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:47.660
Oh, yeah. I think Aigasa-sensei 
had a crush on Oda-kun, too.

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:52.660
She went through a real rough patch when 
Oda-kun and Suzuka-san started dating.

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:55.140
"I can never write again," she told me.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:57.290
It was quite a feat trying to calm her down.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:01.440
And your attempts to comfort 
the desperate Rika-san

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:04.300
shifted her romantic attention to you?

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:07.120
Did you realize it?

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:08.450
Vaguely.

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:10.760
But I had no intention of reciprocating.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:13.060
Certainly not after what happened...

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:15.060
What happened?

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:18.040
She learned about my wife's pregnancy

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.820
and burst into the editorial 
department in a fit.

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:23.800
Then the reason you left 
the light novel department...

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:26.150
Yeah, it was because of that.

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:29.320
And so, to get things under control...

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:34.580
You solicited the help of Rika-san's 
friends, Suzuka-san and Kumi-san?

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:35.980
Yeah.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:40.090
They've been really helpful 
in advising me since then.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:41.590
I understand.

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.000
That's all I wanted to ask.

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:46.010
What do you think, Holmes-san?

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:48.160
Let's see. I still need to...

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:50.690
Yagashira-san! Emergency!

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:51.680
What is it?

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.520
I'm not taking part in this farce anymore.

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:04.530
Damn it! Let me go!

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:07.720
May I ask you just one question?

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:11.000
If it's about my investigation, then no.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:14.040
That's protected by client privilege.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:17.320
Aigasa-sensei commissioned you twice

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:20.170
for background checks on
 people gathered here tonight.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:24.000
The first was on two people.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.490
The second was on one person.

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:26.340
Is that correct?

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:29.340
I-I told you that's confidential.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:31.850
Thank you very much.

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:41.350
I now know everything I need to.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:42.860
So then...

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:49.820
Do you really know who did it?

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:51.110
You could say that.

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.990
At least, I have a theory about 
what I think might have happened.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:55.870
I have no proof, after all.

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:57.700
That's fine.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:58.870
Please tell us!

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.370
Understood.

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:02.860
Then, before I unravel events 
around the incident,

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:07.080
could you tell me about the 
note that Rika-san left?

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.380
B-But... well...

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:12.840
The note was a confession, wasn't it?

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:17.140
That's why you believed she 
really tried to kill herself.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:24.650
"I, Aigasa Kurisu, have 
been deceiving my readers.

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:29.900
The story I had published 
wasn't written by me."

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:33.160
<i>So... she had a ghostwriter?</i>

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:34.810
But it's a lie!

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:38.650
I saw how hard she worked!

00:15:38.650 --> 00:15:42.700
So I know... it can't be true!

00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:46.670
I'm sorry, but I believe it is the truth.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:48.400
No...

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:51.160
At least... partially.

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:53.930
Let's say it's two-thirds true.

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:57.280
Two-thirds?

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:01.670
I believe "Aigasa Kurisu" was originally 
a combination of the names of three people

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:04.800
who admired Agatha Christie: 
Suzuka-san, Kumi-san, and Rika-san.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:08.190
A collective pen name for the three of you.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:11.880
Inoue Rika

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:11.880
Iijima Suzuka

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:11.880
Ooishi Kumi

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:14.400
That turned "Agatha" into "Aigasa" 
because your names all had "I" in them.

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:15.070
Inoue Rika

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:15.070
Iijima Suzuka

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:15.070
Ooishi Kumi

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:18.450
And I believe "Kurisu" was taken from 
the first character in each of your names.

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:18.450
Aigasa Kurisu

00:16:19.030 --> 00:16:22.960
Now, if you will, 
this is my theory based on that.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:26.210
<b>Award

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.990
When Rika-san won the newcomer award,

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:31.210
at first, you were both 
genuinely happy for her.

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:35.900
That was probably the 
best time of your lives.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:40.280
But as Rika-san grew financially well-off

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:42.530
and the two of you became 
more dependent on her,

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:44.850
your relationship began to fray.

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:50.110
Partly due to the guilt she felt about 
using your ideas to get that award,

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:53.780
Rika-san began to feel blackmailed,

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:56.490
thinking she might be your 
slave for the rest of her life.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:57.950
And then...

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:01.750
When Suzuka-san started dating Oda-san,

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.000
those emotions exploded.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.250
<b>Komatsu Detective Agency</b>

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:07.380
Rika-san hired Komatsu-san the detective

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:09.880
to expose your pasts.

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:13.130
Naturally, you were both furious,

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:16.220
and your relationship quickly deteriorated.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:21.640
And with Rika-san in the depths of despair, 
swearing she'd never write again,

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.160
it was Hashimoto-san who comforted her.

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:26.020
Rika-san was your golden goose.

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:29.450
You couldn't afford to lose her so easily.

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:33.250
So you sweet-talked your way into her heart,

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:35.030
and brought her back to life.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:38.530
<b>Komatsu Detective Agency</b>

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:38.530
But a woman's intuition
 is a frightening thing.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.820
Rika-san realized something 
was off about your behavior

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:43.790
and had the detective look into you, too.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:48.040
She found out that you 
had a pregnant fiancée

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:50.950
and flew into a spell once more.

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:55.090
It was then that you remembered 
Suzuka-san and Kumi-san,

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:57.430
and went to them for help.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:04.000
I'm sure that's when you learned "Aigasa Kurisu" 
was once a pen name for the three of them.

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:08.190
And then a wicked idea entered your mind.

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:10.210
A wicked idea?

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:13.030
You thought that if 
Aigasa Kurisu killed herself

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:15.380
and her ghostwriter came forward,

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:18.450
that ghostwriter could 
gain even greater renown.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:20.450
Wait, you mean...

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:21.570
Yes.

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:24.410
Hashimoto-san planned to kill Rika-san

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.690
and make it look like a suicide.

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:29.710
The one who actually carried it out was

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:32.680
either Suzuka-san or Kumi-san, 
who were present at the time.

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:37.360
It was Oda-san who came up 
with the setup for the murder.

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:40.470
Suzuka-san talked you into it, didn't she?

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:46.080
And Kikuchi-san, you witnessed the incident, 
but corroborated Oda-san's story

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.670
because you didn't want to 
get drawn into things, right?

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:50.790
In other words...

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:55.320
Hashimoto-san, Suzuka-san, Kumi-san, 
Oda-san, and Kikuchi-san

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:59.990
were all complicit, 
either directly or indirectly.

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:02.810
E-Enough of this nonsense!

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:05.490
Y-Yeah, you have no proof!

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.400
You want proof?

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:12.500
Perhaps you should ask that 
of the victim herself.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.150
Good day, everyone.

00:19:20.150 --> 00:19:21.510
R-Rika!

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:23.320
Wh-Why...

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:28.580
I've been watching you all through 
the camera in Kana's pendant.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:32.000
And you, Yagashira-san...

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:34.270
I see the rumors about 
your skills aren't just rumors.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:37.650
What will you do now that
 you know the truth?

00:19:38.020 --> 00:19:39.150
Let's see...

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:43.000
Sis!

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:47.800
If I was going to kill myself, 
I think I'd do it with a gun.

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:51.260
Red bloodstains on a black pistol 
would be oh-so beautiful, don't you think?

00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:54.670
Maybe I'll stain you all that lovely color.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.670
Then... I'll turn it on myself.

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:01.440
W-Wait! I just came up with the plan!

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:02.930
It's not my fault!

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:05.470
I-I have nothing to apologize for!

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:09.100
You're the one who hired a 
detective to expose my past!

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:10.930
You started all this!

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:14.480
Y-Yeah! If you want to punish 
someone, punish her!

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:15.810
She's the one who did it!

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:17.960
Th-That's terrible!

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:19.780
You said that if I did what you told me,

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:23.290
you'd publish me as the new Aigasa Kurisu!

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:25.070
That's why I did it!

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:28.000
You idiot, that was just a line.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.180
N-No way...

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:33.160
The likes of you could 
never be Rika's successor.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:35.580
I had another author to follow her up with.

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:41.640
You're awful... I shouldn't have slept 
with this guy just because Rika liked him!

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:46.090
You had everything anyway! 
What's the big deal?!

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:48.760
Suzuka-san, tell me that's not true! Tell me!

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:51.480
Shut up! I don't want to hear
 anything from you!

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:52.850
<i>This is hell...</i>

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:54.850
That's enough.

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.350
Now die.

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:01.860
No way!

00:21:02.100 --> 00:21:04.810
Thank goodness things didn't get ugly.

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:09.370
It doesn't hurt?

00:21:09.590 --> 00:21:12.270
Of course not. This is a toy.

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:15.870
I just wanted to hear
 how all of you really felt.

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:19.130
I've recorded everything 
that was said here today.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:24.130
I'll have to think carefully about whether 
I turn you over to the police or not.

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:27.070
Go on. Get out.

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:28.640
Get going already!

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:30.760
Hey, don't push me!

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:36.450
What a Valentine's Day 
this turned out to be.

00:21:36.450 --> 00:21:37.860
Valentine's...

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:42.150
Sorry, I meant to give these to you!

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:46.590
Sherlock Holmes chocolates?

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:50.030
Because you're the Holmes of Kyoto!

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:52.190
Thank you very much.

00:21:52.190 --> 00:21:54.740
It's a wonderful birthday present.

00:21:55.530 --> 00:21:57.260
B-Birthday?

00:21:57.260 --> 00:22:00.540
February 14th is my birthday.

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:02.960
R-Really?

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:06.870
I wish I'd gotten you a present...

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:10.550
Though it probably would have
 been something silly

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:12.810
like the handmade cookies 
I gave you for Christmas...

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:14.540
Those weren't silly!

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:16.310
H-Holmes-san?

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:20.040
Those cookies were superb.

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:21.810
They weren't silly at all.

00:22:25.050 --> 00:22:27.140
Um, Aoi-san...

00:22:27.140 --> 00:22:30.570
You don't dislike me, do you?

00:22:32.090 --> 00:22:34.100
When our hands touched earlier,

00:22:34.100 --> 00:22:36.160
you pulled back so quickly...

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:38.550
I thought you might hate me so much

00:22:38.550 --> 00:22:39.830
that you hate even touching me...

00:22:39.830 --> 00:22:41.830
Th-That's not it at all!

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:46.840
<i>Is my decision to draw a line
 showing in my behavior?</i>

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:49.440
Holmes-san!

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:51.840
Let's... Let's shake hands!

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:56.350
See? I don't dislike touching you at all.

00:22:56.350 --> 00:22:58.920
I'm... glad to hear that.

00:22:59.580 --> 00:23:02.450
B-By the way, Holmes-san...

00:23:02.450 --> 00:23:05.440
You had something to give 
me earlier, didn't you?

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:06.890
Oh, yes.

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:15.600
Are these appraiser's gloves?

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:19.440
Yes, to celebrate your being 
able to drink black coffee.

00:23:19.950 --> 00:23:24.940
And more importantly, now that 
you've matured as an appraiser,

00:23:24.940 --> 00:23:27.380
I thought you could use them.

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:32.140
They're wonderful!

00:23:32.140 --> 00:23:34.360
I'll really treasure them.

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.400
"Conditions of an Heir"

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.400
Next Episode

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:39.960
I've been working at Kura 
for a year now, I guess.

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:42.450
Though it feels more like three months.

00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:47.400
Next time: "Conditions of an Heir."

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:49.470
Holmes-san, you really are nasty.
